    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36950" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏlyrrhīzos</span></b> ,
		on, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύρριζος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Having many roots</i>, an appellation of several
			plants, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 8, 54</span></i>, §§
			96, 98 al.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏlyrrhīzon</span></b> , i,
				n., <i>a plant</i>, otherwise unknown,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				27, 12, 103, § 126</span></i>.</div>
